\tag{fdip}
\title{Slabs and exact boundary modes}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{The mass in the [Wilson operator](fdip-009U) distinguishes
transverse Fourier corners. If two ends of a periodic direction
are cut apart, which fields can vanish under the operator while
remaining on a single face? How does the answer depend on the
periods and on the links between layers?}

